@format 1
@id section-naming.pending-inline-commit
@title Commit pending inline name before another action
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry delete-click,sort-click,badge-double-click,other-row-single-click
@summary Show Split Sections-panel operations that call PSectionEditCommit first, causing a pending inline name/prefix/suffix edit to be applied before the non-naming action proceeds.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-input, section-naming.common.apply-name-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag name
@tag rename
@tag implicit-commit

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection

[delete-click] Delete button Click <input>
~ This starts with delete button Click.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionDeleteHandle calls PSectionEditCommit before PFlowSectionDelete continues outside naming @ panel.PSectionDeleteHandle(...)
> commit-entry

[sort-click] Sort button Click <input>
~ This starts with sort button Click.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionSortHandle calls PSectionEditCommit before PFlowSectionSort continues outside naming @ panel.PSectionSortHandle(...)
> commit-entry

[badge-double-click] Color badge MouseLeftButtonDown double-click <input>
~ This starts when the user double-clicks the section color badge.
[Technical explanation]
- The color badge MouseLeftButtonDown path releases capture, clears drag state, and calls PSectionEditCommit before toggling @ panel.PSectionRowBuild(...) / color badge MouseLeftButtonDown
> commit-entry

[other-row-single-click] Mouse-up after clicking another row <input>
~ This starts with mouse-up after clicking another row.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionUpHandle calls PSectionEditCommit when the click did not become a drag and the clicked row differs from the editing row; selection follows after the commit returns @ panel.PSectionUpHandle(...)
> commit-entry

[commit-entry] Pending commit calls converge <junction>
> editor-check

[editor-check] Inline editor active <decision>
~ The program checks inline editor active.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditCommit returns unless pSectionIndexEditing and the main-name TextBox are both available @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
? "No active editor" > no-naming-effect
? "Editor active" > snapshot

[no-naming-effect] Continue other action <output>
~ This path ends with continue other action.
[Technical explanation]
= No naming mutation occurs.

[snapshot] Trim and clear editor state <process>
~ This step handles trim and clear editor state.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditCommit trims name/prefix/suffix, clears the editing index and tracked TextBoxes, calls PFlowNameSet, and after it returns PSectionEditCommit rebuilds the Sections panel before the originating action continues @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
> map:section-naming.common.apply-name-state
